WEBVTT

00:59:58.776 --> 01:00:01.182
What decade, exactly,
do people want to go back to?

01:00:01.206 --> 01:00:03.215
I wouldn't want to go back to any of them.

01:00:03.239 --> 01:00:04.775
I think our problems are severe,

01:00:04.799 --> 01:00:07.046
and global warming
and things are really severe,

01:00:07.070 --> 01:00:10.520
but I'd rather have our problems
than almost any other decade's problems.

01:00:10.544 --> 01:00:12.483
One of the things I think about a lot --

01:00:12.507 --> 01:00:14.890
and I haven't really taken
this thought very far --

01:00:14.914 --> 01:00:17.789
is that we've spent a lot of time,
all of us in our business,

01:00:17.813 --> 01:00:20.957
thinking about decision-making
and cognitive biases and heuristics

01:00:20.981 --> 01:00:22.501
and the work of Danny Kahneman.

01:00:22.525 --> 01:00:25.366
And over the last 30 years,
we've learned so much about that

01:00:25.390 --> 01:00:27.085
and just how we do decisions.

01:00:27.109 --> 01:00:30.193
The next big frontier,
it seems to me, is desire.